[62.197969, "o", "{\"type\":\"assistant\",\"message\":{\"model\":\"claude-sonnet-4-6\",\"id\":\"msg_01B9H5TYXogcxF1TCBqiES7Q\",\"type\":\"message\",\"role\":\"assistant\",\"content\":[{\"type\":\"thinking\",\"thinking\":\"Now I have a complete picture. Let me write the visual gaps report.\\n\\nKey findings:\\n\\n**Algorithms in src/ vs UI:**\\nAll 10 exported finders are present in UI. But JumpPointFinder has 4 diagonal movement modes - only 2 are exposed:\\n- `DiagonalMovement.IfAtMostOneObstacle` → \\\"Jump Point Search\\\" ✓\\n- `DiagonalMovement.Never` → \\\"Orthogonal Jump Point Search\\\" ✓\\n- `DiagonalMovement.Always` → NOT exposed ✗\\n\\n\\n- `DiagonalMovement.OnlyWhenNoObstacles` → NOT exposed ✗\\n\\n**Bugs/issues:**\\nThe coordinate conversion in view.js works correctly since the draw area is positioned at the viewport origin with no margins. For the IDA* weight spinner, there's a naming inconsistency where it uses the A* parameter name, but the selector properly scopes it to the IDA* section so it functions as intended.\\n\\nThere's a CSS typo in the ho"]
[62.198046, "o", "ver state for the hide instructions button that breaks the styling. The controller has outdated comments referencing non-existent drawing states, and several hardcoded values lack UI controls: animation speed is fixed at 300 ops/sec, grid dimensions are locked at 64×36, and there's no way to adjust these without code changes. The parent pointer visualization is marked as a TODO and isn't implemented. The \\\"Clear Walls\\\" button performs a full reset instead of just clearing walls.\\n\\nBeyond these bugs, there are missing features: no mobile or touch support, no maze generation, no algorithm comparison mode, and stats only display after search finishes rather than updating live. The hide instructions button has no corresponding show mechanism, so once hidden the instructions disappear permanently. The weight spinner accepts arbitrarily large values with no upper limit, and the BiIDA* option is correctly absent since that algorithm isn't implemented in the library.\\n\\nNow I'm writing up the full report.\",\"signat"]
