[62.19829, "o", ":null,\"usage\":{\"input_tokens\":1,\"cache_creation_input_tokens\":2102,\"cache_read_input_tokens\":36513,\"cache_creation\":{\"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens\":0,\"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens\":2102},\"output_tokens\":24,\"service_tier\":\"standard\",\"inference_geo\":\"not_available\"},\"context_management\":null},\"parent_tool_use_id\":null,\"session_id\":\"796930c1-378a-44eb-9017-806bd4c6a53b\",\"uuid\":\"f3c88c83-9542-4f3c-958b-502b560e3cdf\"}\r\n"]
[62.203053, "o", "{\"type\":\"assistant\",\"message\":{\"model\":\"claude-sonnet-4-6\",\"id\":\"msg_01B9H5TYXogcxF1TCBqiES7Q\",\"type\":\"message\",\"role\":\"assistant\",\"content\":[{\"type\":\"text\",\"text\":\"Now I have enough. Writing report.\"}],\"stop_reason\":null,\"stop_sequence\":null,\"stop_details\":null,\"usage\":{\"input_tokens\":1,\"cache_creation_input_tokens\":2102,\"cache_read_input_tokens\":36513,\"cache_creation\":{\"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens\":0,\"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens\":2102},\"output_tokens\":24,\"service_tier\":\"standard\",\"inference_geo\":\"not_available\"},\"context_management\":null},\"parent_tool_use_id\":null,\"session_id\":\"796930c1-378a-44eb-9017-806bd4c6a53b\",\"uuid\":\"9fd52e81-5156-43d4-9edf-e5e24d33e265\"}\r\n"]
[115.616304, "o", "{\"type\":\"assistant\",\"message\":{\"model\":\"claude-sonnet-4-6\",\"id\":\"msg_01B9H5TYXogcxF1TCBqiES7Q\",\"type\":\"message\",\"role\":\"assistant\",\"content\":[{\"type\":\"tool_use\",\"id\":\"toolu_01XjkbbHwHNbmT78NtKCF9ru\",\"name\":\"Write\",\"input\":{\"file_path\":\"/home/sagar/template-repo/docs/experiments/001-demo-artifacts/fleets/fleet-01-test-blitz/workers/visual-auditor/output/visual-gaps.md\",\"content\":\"# Visual Demo Audit Report\\n\\n## Current Visual App Capabilities\\n\\n| Feature | Details |\\n|---------|---------|\\n| Grid | 64×36 fixed, SVG via Raphael.js |\\n| Draw obstacles | Click-drag on white cells |\\n| Erase obstacles | Click-drag on grey cells |\\n| Drag start node | Green node, draggable in ready/finished states |\\n| Drag end node | Red (orange) node, draggable in ready/finished states |\\n| Algorithm selection | Accordion panel (right side), 7 accordion sections |\\n| Start/Pause/Resume/Cancel | 3-button panel below algorithm panel |\\n| Restart Search | Available during searching/finished states |\\n| Clear Walls | Full reset (c"]
[115.617192, "o", "lears path, walls, and rebuilds grid) |\\n| Stats display | Path length, time (ms), operation count — shown after search completes |\\n| Visualization | Opened nodes (green), closed nodes (teal), tested nodes (grey), path (yellow line) |\\n| Instructions panel | Dismissible, not re-showable once hidden |\\n| State machine | 12-state FSM via javascript-state-machine |\\n\\n---\\n\\n## Algorithms: Available vs Exposed in UI\\n\\n### Fully Exposed ✓\\n\\n| Algorithm | UI Section | Bi-directional | Heuristics | Options |\\n|-----------|-----------|----------------|------------|---------|\\n| A* | `astar_header` | ✓ (checkbox → BiAStarFinder) | Manhattan, Euclidean, Octile, Chebyshev | Allow Diagonal, Don't Cross Corners, Weight |\\n| IDA* | `ida_header` | ✗ (no BiIDA* exists) | Manhattan, Euclidean, Octile, Chebyshev | Allow Diagonal, Don't Cross Corners, Weight, Time Limit, Visualize Recursion |\\n| Breadth-First Search | `breadthfirst_header` | ✓ (checkbox → BiBreadthFirstFinder) | — | Allow Diagonal, Don't Cro"]
[115.617255, "o", "ss Corners |\\n| Best-First Search | `bestfirst_header` | ✓ (checkbox → BiBestFirstFinder) | Manhattan, Euclidean, Octile, Chebyshev | Allow Diagonal, Don't Cross Corners |\\n| Dijkstra | `dijkstra_header` | ✓ (checkbox → BiDijkstraFinder) | — | Allow Diagonal, Don't Cross Corners |\\n| Jump Point Search | `jump_point_header` | — | Manhattan, Euclidean, Octile, Chebyshev | Visualize Recursion |\\n| Orthogonal Jump Point Search | `orth_jump_point_header` | — | Manhattan, Euclidean, Octile, Chebyshev | Visualize Recursion |\\n\\n### Missing from UI ✗\\n\\n| Algorithm | Reason Missing |\\n|-----------|---------------|\\n| `JumpPointFinder` with `DiagonalMovement.Always` | `JPFAlwaysMoveDiagonally` — no UI section |\\n| `JumpPointFinder` with `DiagonalMovement.OnlyWhenNoObstacles` | `JPFMoveDiagonallyIfNoObstacles` — no UI section |\\n\\n**Note:** `JumpPointFinder` is a factory dispatching to 4 implementations based on `diagonalMovement`. UI exposes only 2 of 4 modes. The other 2 (`Always`, `OnlyWhenNoObst"]
[115.617281, "o", "acles`) are in the compiled browser bundle but unreachable.\\n\\n---\\n\\n## Bugs and Broken Features\\n\\n### Bug 1 — CSS hover selector typo (`style.css:59`)\\n```css\\n/* BROKEN — selector missing 's' */\\n#hide_instruction:hover { ... }\\n/* Should be */\\n#hide_instructions:hover { ... }\\n```\\nHover style on the \\\"hide\\\" link never applies.\\n\\n### Bug 2 — Instructions panel cannot be re-shown\\n`#hide_instructions` click calls `slideUp()`. No mechanism to show it again. Once dismissed, instructions are gone for the session.\\n\\n### Bug 3 — \\\"Clear Walls\\\" label is misleading (`controller.js:219`)\\nButton labeled \\\"Clear Walls\\\" calls `this.reset`, which triggers `onreset` → `clearAll()` + `buildNewGrid()`. It clears **everything** (walls + path + footprints), not just walls. User expectation vs actual behavior mismatch.\\n\\n### Bug 4 — IDA* weight spinner has wrong `name` attribute (`index.html:103`)\\n```html\\n<input class=\\\"spinner\\\" name=\\\"astar_weight\\\" value=\\\"1\\\">  <!-- inside #ida_section -->\\n```\\nS"]
[115.617304, "o", "hould be `name=\\\"ida_weight\\\"` or similar. The panel.js selector `$('#ida_section input[name=astar_weight]')` scopes correctly so it works, but it's a copy-paste bug that would break if the selector were ever changed to be global.\\n\\n### Bug 5 — `parent` attribute visualization missing (`view.js:170`)\\n```js\\ncase 'parent':\\n    // XXX: Maybe draw a line from this node to its parent?\\n    break;\\n```\\nParent pointers are tracked in operations but never rendered. No parent-pointer arrows shown during search.\\n\\n### Gap 6 — Animation speed hardcoded (`controller.js:95`)\\n```js\\noperationsPerSecond: 300,\\n```\\nNo slider or UI control exposed. Users cannot slow down to study algorithm behavior or speed up for large grids.\\n\\n### Gap 7 — Grid size hardcoded (`controller.js:94`)\\n```js\\ngridSize: [64, 36],\\n```\\nNo UI to resize the grid. Small grids would be more useful for slow algorithms (IDA*). Large grids would stress-test JPS.\\n\\n### Gap 8 — No random maze generator\\nNo \\\"Generate Maze\\\" button. Users "]
[115.617327, "o", "must draw obstacles manually. Standard maze-generation algorithms (recursive backtracking, Prim's) would significantly improve demo utility.\\n\\n### Gap 9 — No touch/mobile support\\nOnly `mousedown`, `mousemove`, `mouseup` events bound (`controller.js:339–343`). No `touchstart`/`touchmove`/`touchend` equivalents. Demo is unusable on mobile.\\n\\n### Gap 10 — Stats not shown during search\\n`View.showStats()` only called in `onfinish` (`controller.js:174`). No live operation counter during animation.\\n\\n### Gap 11 — JPS diagonal mode not user-configurable\\n\\\"Jump Point Search\\\" section hardcodes `DiagonalMovement.IfAtMostOneObstacle` (`panel.js:138`). User cannot select between `Always`, `OnlyWhenNoObstacles`, or `IfAtMostOneObstacle` — even though all three are in the bundle. Orthogonal JPS is a separate hard-coded section.\\n\\n### Gap 12 — No algorithm comparison / side-by-side mode\\nOnly one algorithm runs at a time. No way to visually compare node expansion between A* and Dijkstra, or JPS vs BFS.\\n\\"]
[115.617352, "o", "n### Gap 13 — Weight spinner has no upper bound validation in UI\\nIDA* and A* weight spinners accept any integer. Extremely large weights make weighted A* degenerate but the UI shows no warning.\\n\\n---\\n\\n## Suggested Visual Test Scenarios\\n\\n### Scenario 1 — Open Grid (No Obstacles)\\n- **Setup:** Default 64×36 grid, start left-center, end right-center, no walls\\n- **Run:** All algorithms\\n- **Expected:** A*/BFS/Dijkstra find same-length optimal path; JPS expands far fewer nodes; IDA* may time out on large grid\\n- **Validates:** Basic path drawing, stats accuracy, node coloring\\n\\n### Scenario 2 — Blocked Grid (No Path)\\n- **Setup:** Solid wall column between start and end\\n- **Run:** All algorithms\\n- **Expected:** No path drawn, stats show length=0 or path absent, UI returns to `finished` state cleanly\\n- **Validates:** No-path edge case, stats display when path is empty\\n\\n### Scenario 3 — Diagonal vs Orthogonal\\n- **Setup:** Start top-left, end bottom-right, no walls\\n- **Run:** A* Manhattan diag"]
[115.61737, "o", "onal-allowed vs A* Manhattan diagonal-disallowed\\n- **Expected:** Diagonal path is shorter (√2 vs 2 per step); orthogonal path hugs axes\\n- **Validates:** `allowDiagonal` checkbox wires correctly to finder\\n\\n### Scenario 4 — Don't Cross Corners\\n- **Setup:** Diagonal corridor that requires corner-cutting to traverse\\n- **Run:** A* with diagonal allowed, corners-cross enabled vs disabled\\n- **Expected:** With `dontCrossCorners=true`, path routes around; with `false`, path cuts corner\\n- **Validates:** Corner-crossing option propagates to finder\\n\\n### Scenario 5 — Bi-directional Toggle\\n- **Setup:** Long open corridor\\n- **Run:** A* unidirectional vs bidirectional (same heuristic)\\n- **Expected:** Bi-directional expands roughly half the nodes; both find same path length\\n- **Validates:** Bi-directional checkbox switches to `BiAStarFinder`\\n\\n### Scenario 6 — IDA* Time Limit\\n- **Setup:** Complex maze, time limit set to 1 second\\n- **Run:** IDA*\\n- **Expected:** Search terminates at time limit; partial"]
[115.617387, "o", " recursion visualized if `track_recursion` checked\\n- **Validates:** `timeLimit` option wires through; UI handles early-termination finish state\\n\\n### Scenario 7 — JPS vs A* Node Expansion\\n- **Setup:** Large open grid, diagonal allowed\\n- **Run:** JPS then A* (same heuristic)\\n- **Expected:** JPS \\\"jumps\\\" with far fewer colored nodes; A* fills much more of the grid\\n- **Validates:** JPS visualization shows jump recursion correctly when toggle enabled\\n\\n### Scenario 8 — Drag Start/End During Finished State\\n- **Setup:** Run any algorithm to completion\\n- **Expected behavior:** Drag start or end node → state transitions to `modified` → UI shows \\\"Start Search\\\" / \\\"Clear Path\\\" buttons\\n- **Validates:** `modify` state transition, button re-labeling\\n\\n### Scenario 9 — Pause and Resume\\n- **Run:** A* on large open grid (many operations to visualize)\\n- **Pause mid-animation**, then Resume\\n- **Expected:** Animation stops exactly, resumes from same position, no duplicate operations\\n- **Validates:**"]
[115.617406, "o", " `loop()` / `pause` / `resume` state transitions\\n\\n### Scenario 10 — Weight > 1 (Weighted A*)\\n- **Setup:** Open grid, A* with weight=5 vs weight=1\\n- **Run:** Both\\n- **Expected:** Higher weight produces faster but potentially suboptimal path (fewer nodes expanded)\\n- **Validates:** Weight spinner parsed and applied to finder\\n\\n### Scenario 11 — Orthogonal JPS vs BFS (No Diagonal)\\n- **Setup:** Grid with obstacles, `DiagonalMovement.Never`\\n- **Run:** Orthogonal JPS vs BFS\\n- **Expected:** Both find same "]
[115.617601, "o", "path; JPS expands fewer nodes; path is purely cardinal-direction steps\\n- **Validates:** `JPFNeverMoveDiagonally` path correctness\\n\\n### Scenario 12 — Start == End (Degenerate)\\n- **Setup:** Drag end node onto start node position (or vice versa) — if UI allows\\n- **Expected:** Immediate finish with path length 0, no crash\\n- **Validates:** Edge case path-length=0 handling\\n\\n---\\n\\n## Summary\\n\\n| Category | Count |\\n|----------|-------|\\n| Algorithms fully exposed | 10 (all exported) |\\n| JPS dia"]
[115.617652, "o", "gonal modes missing from UI | 2 of 4 |\\n| Confirmed bugs | 5 |\\n| UX gaps | 8 |\\n| Suggested test scenarios | 12 |\\n\"},\"caller\":{\"type\":\"direct\"}}],\"stop_reason\":null,\"stop_sequence\":null,\"stop_details\":null,\"usage\":{\"input_tokens\":1,\"cache_creation_input_tokens\":2102,\"cache_read_input_tokens\":36513,\"cache_creation\":{\"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens\":0,\"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens\":2102},\"output_tokens\":24,\"service_tier\":\"standard\",\"inference_geo\":\"not_available\"},\"context_management\":null},\"parent_tool_use_id\":null,\"session_id\":\"796930c1-378a-44eb-9017-806bd4c6a53b\",\"uuid\":\"d1a86c70-2f87-4f70-bc77-50be288c8f03\"}"]
